# Allow-list: exclude everything, then re-include only the files the
# root Dockerfile COPYs. A deny-list misses untracked local files
# (.claude/, CLAUDE.local.md, .netrc, ...) and its root-only globs do
# not match in subdirectories, so those files would reach the build
# context. If you add a COPY/ADD to the Dockerfile, add a matching `!`
# line here, or the build fails with "not found".
*
!entrypoint.sh
!lib.sh
!openssl-tls12.cnf
!VERSION
